00:33:22.525 --> 00:33:43.091
ADR-053 Kafka as the event backbone; ADR-054 Keys, partitions and naming; ADR-055 Durability settings; ADR-056 Retry topics and DLT ownership; ADR-057 Avro + schema registry (backward).

578
00:33:44.441 --> 00:33:45.081
1.

579
00:33:45.361 --> 00:33:46.769
Context and Problem.

580
00:33:47.049 --> 00:34:04.371
Unkeyed events reordered order state for 1,900 orders, a poison message stalled invoicing for 4 h, eager rebalances delayed SMS by 40 min, and acks=1 lost ~3,000 acknowledged events (§1.1).

581
00:34:04.651 --> 00:34:05.355
2.

582
00:34:05.635 --> 00:34:06.979
Goals or Non-Goals.

583
00:34:07.259 --> 00:34:25.755
Goals: per-order ordering; no acknowledged event lost on single-broker or single-AZ failure; a poison message never stalls a partition for more than its retry budget; lag p99 5 s at peak for tier-1 consumers; schemas evolve without breaking consumers.

584
00:34:27.105 --> 00:34:37.815
Non-goals: exactly-once to external systems (handled by idempotent consumers, Ch 13); cross-region active-active streaming (Ch 27).

585
00:34:38.095 --> 00:34:38.841
3.

586
00:34:39.121 --> 00:34:40.081
Requirements.

587
00:34:41.431 --> 00:34:42.797
Here is a quick table:

588
00:34:43.077 --> 00:34:44.549
ID, and Requirement.

589
00:34:44.829 --> 00:34:45.874
NFR-1:

590
00:34:46.154 --> 00:34:51.039
RPO 0 for acknowledged events on loss of one broker or one AZ.

591
00:34:51.319 --> 00:34:52.365
NFR-2:

592
00:34:52.645 --> 00:34:55.503
Per-aggregate ordering for every order. topic.

593
00:34:55.783 --> 00:34:56.850
NFR-3:

594
00:34:57.130 --> 00:35:08.586
Tier-1 consumer lag (time) p99 5 s; alert at 60 s; retention ≥ 7 days (≥ 100x the alert).

595
00:35:08.866 --> 00:35:09.954
NFR-4:

596
00:35:10.234 --> 00:35:17.743
Non-retryable failures reach the DLT on first failure; retryable ones within 3 attempts over at most 5 min.

597
00:35:18.023 --> 00:35:19.069
NFR-5:

598
00:35:19.349 --> 00:35:24.533
Schema changes are backward compatible, enforced in CI and by the registry.

599
00:35:24.813 --> 00:35:25.901
NFR-6:

600
00:35:26.181 --> 00:35:29.765
Rolling restarts don't trigger rebalances (static membership).

601
00:35:31.115 --> 00:35:31.819
4.

602
00:35:32.099 --> 00:35:34.211
Capacity and latency estimates.

603
00:35:35.561 --> 00:35:36.926
Here is a quick table:

604
00:35:37.206 --> 00:35:39.510
Item, and Calculation, and Result.

605
00:35:39.790 --> 00:35:41.667
Order events at P90 peak.

606
00:35:41.947 --> 00:35:47.046
Calculation: ~420 orders per second times ~3 events.

607
00:35:47.326 --> 00:35:50.270
Result: ~1.3 K events per second.

608
00:35:50.550 --> 00:35:51.339
Bytes.

609
00:35:51.619 --> 00:35:55.011
Calculation: ~1 KB Avro + headers.

610
00:35:55.291 --> 00:35:58.001
Result: ~1.3 MB per second.

611
00:35:58.281 --> 00:35:59.155
Storage.

612
00:35:59.435 --> 00:36:00.502
Calculation:

613
00:36:00.782 --> 00:36:09.209
1.3 MB per second times 86,400 times 7 days times RF 3 times 1.2.

614
00:36:09.489 --> 00:36:12.987
Result: ~2.8 TB (all order topics).

615
00:36:13.267 --> 00:36:15.977
Partitions for order.order.placed.v1.

616
00:36:16.257 --> 00:36:17.323
Calculation:

617
00:36:17.603 --> 00:36:28.526
Peak 420 per second; slowest consumer ~25 ms or record, then 40 per second per consumer, then 11 consumers; times 2 headroom.

618
00:36:28.806 --> 00:36:29.617
Result:

619
00:36:29.897 --> 00:36:30.899
24.

620
00:36:31.179 --> 00:36:34.230
Produce latency (acks=all, cross-AZ).

621
00:36:34.510 --> 00:36:35.577
Calculation:

622
00:36:35.857 --> 00:36:39.569
Leader append + follower fetch round trip ~1 to 3 ms.

623
00:36:39.849 --> 00:36:42.281
Result: p99 ~10 ms.

624
00:36:42.561 --> 00:36:44.289
Failover (leader election).

625
00:36:44.569 --> 00:36:45.635
Calculation:

626
00:36:45.915 --> 00:36:48.795
KRaft controller + metadata propagation.

627
00:36:49.075 --> 00:36:52.382
Result: ~1 to 5 s of NOTLEADER retries.

628
00:36:53.732 --> 00:36:54.500
5.

629
00:36:54.780 --> 00:36:55.975
Proposed design.

630
00:36:56.255 --> 00:37:04.319
Naming: domain.entity.event.vN, with retry topics topic.retry-delay and the DLT topic.dlt.

631
00:37:04.599 --> 00:37:07.372
One event type per topic for high-volume events.

632
00:37:07.652 --> 00:37:11.279
Low-volume related events may share a topic with a type header.

633
00:37:11.559 --> 00:37:15.143
Keys: the aggregate id (orderid, storeid:sku, riderid).

634
00:37:15.423 --> 00:37:21.951
Partition counts are fixed at creation with headroom; a repartition means a new topic + dual publish.

635
00:37:23.301 --> 00:37:24.261
Durability:

636
00:37:24.541 --> 00:37:31.389
RF 3 across 3 AZs (rack-aware), min.insync.replicas=2, unclean election off.

637
00:37:31.669 --> 00:37:38.815
Producers use acks=all, idempotence on, delivery.timeout.ms=120000.

638
00:37:39.095 --> 00:37:57.378
Consumers: cooperative-sticky (or the KIP-848 protocol), static membership, max.poll.records sized so a batch completes in 30 % of max.poll.interval.ms, manual commits after processing, and idempotent effects (inbox, Ch 13).

639
00:37:58.728 --> 00:37:59.581
Errors:

640
00:37:59.861 --> 00:38:10.528
Spring Kafka DefaultErrorHandler with a classifier, non-blocking retries (10s, 2m) for retryable errors, straight to the DLT for non-retryable ones.

641
00:38:10.808 --> 00:38:14.541
Every DLT has an owner, an alert and a replay CLI.

642
00:38:14.821 --> 00:38:15.696
Schemas:

643
00:38:15.976 --> 00:38:18.941
Avro with the registry in BACKWARDTRANSITIVE mode.

644
00:38:19.221 --> 00:38:26.155
Contract tests in CI (Ch 29), and a new.vN+1 topic for breaking changes.

645
00:38:26.435 --> 00:38:37.016
Compacted topics for latest state feeds (stock, prices), with a min.compaction.lag.ms that lets consumers see intermediate values if they need them.

646
00:38:37.296 --> 00:38:38.043
